# Real credentials — never commit these
secrets.json
/secrets.json
**/secrets.json

# Wrangler local state — never commit these.
# Two reasons, the second one matters a great deal:
#   1. It caches the Cloudflare account id and other machine-local tooling state.
#   2. `wrangler dev` SIMULATES KV ON DISK UNDERNEATH THIS FOLDER. Anyone who runs it against
#      the HR routes would leave real HR data — salaries, employee records — sitting in the
#      working tree, one `git add .` away from a PUBLIC repo with permanent history.
# HR data lives in Cloudflare KV and nowhere else. This line is part of enforcing that.
.wrangler/
**/.wrangler/

# Static build output (regenerated by build-static.ps1 / CI; never committed)
site/
site_*/

# Throwaway test/verification scripts from setup (safe to delete locally)
_test_*.ps1

# Overtime probe scratch output
ot-probe/

# Scratch / temp / logs
scratch/
tmp/
*.log

# NOTE: do NOT ignore data/*.json — those frozen day/month snapshots are
# committed on purpose; the deployed site serves them.
#
# NOTE: do NOT ignore data/last-refresh.txt — the CI heartbeat file MUST commit
# on every run so the scheduled workflow keeps showing activity (GitHub disables
# schedules after 60 days of inactivity). Nothing here excludes it.
scratch_*.ps1
